WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:25.714
Heating systems keep people alive in winter. You need to know them cold.

00:00:25.714 --> 00:00:51.429
Complete furnace inspection lab covering visual heat exchanger inspection, flame
sensor cleaning and microamp measurement, igniter resistance check, gas pressure
measurement, burner flame inspection, blower amp draw, filter replacement,

00:00:51.429 --> 00:01:17.143
Here are the key terms. Write these down.

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:42.857
Temperature Rise: Supply minus return air temp across furnace. Must be within
nameplate range.

00:01:42.857 --> 00:02:08.571
Here's why this matters on the job: Furnace maintenance is major revenue for
HVAC companies.

00:02:08.571 --> 00:02:34.286
Watch out for these: Check temperature rise against nameplate range. And — Flame
sensor below 1 microamp needs cleaning

00:02:34.286 --> 00:03:00.000
Take a minute before you move on. What's the one thing from this lesson you need
to remember on a service call?

